	)
	(text "SW10 OFF (A): LID_SW low, the firmware holds the lid bridge off (coast): plug or unplug it like this.\nSW10 ON (C): LID_SW high (pull-up), heater enabled; D11 red lit.  The lid buck runs whenever +24V is up.\nJ20 (JST PH 7, side entry, top edge): 1 + 7 GND, 2 LID_24V (F2), 3 SDA1, 4 SCL1, 5 IN1, 6 IN2;\nR29-R32 100 R in series; D13 ESD array at the port; R73/R74 Wire1 pull-ups (2k2).  Hot-plugging the lid is safe."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 99.06 320.04 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 1.27 1.27))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b90b6e53-b33f-4d74-8cdd-86463b83186a")
	)
	(text "LED DIMMER: 2-channel linear constant-current sink; set-point = filtered Teensy PWM, so the LEDs see DC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 165.1 177.8 0)
		(effects
