	(text "OFF-BOARD (elsewhere on the unit)\nRail motor: NEMA11 on the rail, direct cable to J3.\nLED strips: COB CCT 24 V on the two chamber walls, joined end to end, to J16."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 713.74 210.82 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 1.524 1.524))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8daf665a-5740-48d7-9b80-3d69477444cb")
	)
	(text "NOTES - operating rules, connector tables and build notes in notes.md\n1. POWER: 24 V barrel jack J15 (centre +) is the only input.  F1 || F3 PTC (2.2 A hold); Q4/Q6 + SW9 = power switch, soft start, reverse block; C12 is where the input lands.\n   v12: ONE ground net.  The board is 4 layers (signal+power / GND / GND / SMT+signal), so every signal has a solid return plane under it; the star is kept by placement (each switching loop local, the input return straight to C12).\n2. COMMS: Ethernet through J19 (transformer-isolated) to a PC or the Raspberry Pi; USB for firmware only.  Earth the 0 V at one place: the PSU.  J19's shell: R76 1M || C67 1 nF 2 kV to GND.\n3. Rail (X coarse): U2 TMC2209 over single-wire UART (TX1 -> R1 1k -> PDN_UART <- RX1); MS1 = MS2 = GND (address 0); CLK = GND (internal clock); SPREAD, STDBY = GND.\n   3 x 1 R sense per coil (0.33 R).  VREF tied to 5VOUT: current from IRUN/IHOLD over UART (I_scale_analog = 0).  EN pulled high (driver off) until firmware enables it.\n4. Fine XYZ: U4/U8/U9 DRV8251A on the DRIVE board (../drive_pcb), on the 9 V rail sent up the 20-way ribbon; PWM from the Teensy (pairs 28/29, 36/37, 24/25) via 1k;\n   IPROPI back down the ribbon to A13/A14/A12 (1k + 10n here); hardware current limit 0.95 A each (VREF from a 9 V divider on the head).\n   V9_OFF (pin 9) high switches the head's 9 V buck off (acquisition): via R77 and ribbon 15 (v15: U3 is on the head, fed 24 V through F4).  Default (reset) = on.\n5. Limits: 8 normally-closed switches on the head.  Rail: separate MIN (home) / MAX.  Fine axes: hi + lo in series.  Closed = LOW; hit or broken wire = HIGH.\n6. Dimmer: set-point = Teensy PWM (23 W, 33 C; ~36.6 kHz, 12 bit) through 10k/15k + 470n, 10k + 470n: 0-1.98 V DC.  I_LED = (V_set - 5 mV) / R_sense\n   (R13/R14 49.9R -> 0-40 mA; two long walls need ~37 mA).  R17/R18 offset IN- ~5 mV: low codes fully dark.  R_in 1k + C_C 100n integrator; R_G 1k; R_GS 100k.\n7. Lid port J20 (JST PH 7: GND on pins 1 and 7): +24V through F2 (the lid makes its own 9 V; v14) + SW10 = heater enable (Teensy pin 41; D11 red = on) + Wire1 (pins 16/17, pull-ups R73/R74 2k2 here) + PWM (pins 14/15), see ../../lid/heating_pcb.\n   The board stands on edge: J3 rail motor (ZH, underside), SW9, SW11, SW10, J20 lid and J16 LED open through the top edge; J15 + J19 at the front end.\n   v20: SW11 = MOTORS: MOT_24V (U2 VS + F4 -> the head) through Q8's soft start; on only while positioning.  MOT_ON (pin 40) reads it.\n8. Teensy VIN = 5 V from U5 through D10 (B5819W).  Cut the Teensy's VUSB-VIN pads and fit a Schottky across them (VUSB -> VIN): a diode-OR, so USB powers the Teensy alone (board off) and neither supply back-feeds the other.\n   The Teensy plugs into 2 x 1x24 sockets (8.5 mm) on the underside.\n9. LEDs: side-view, on the underside at the top edge, shining up, each opposite its switch (v20): D8 green = power (5 V rail) and D9 RGB = status (Teensy pins 10/11/12, active low)\n   at SW9; D16 amber = motors powered (MOT_24V) at SW11; D11 red = lid heater enabled (SW10 on) at SW10."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 420.37 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 1.27 1.27))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e4c5de71-d32e-4b36-83fd-4b3bfbce2ec6")
	)
